{%- comment -%}
  Full-bleed photo hero for the occasion collection template
  (templates/collection.occasion.json) — one section instance serves all
  four occasion collections (slow-mornings, entertaining, sunday-roast,
  high-tea), so every occasion-specific value here comes from the current
  collection's own data (`closest.collection`), nothing hardcoded per
  occasion.

  Not built on sections/hero.liquid: that section's media settings are
  static image_pickers (one fixed image per section instance), which
  can't vary per collection the way this template needs — the same
  section instance renders for four different collections, each needing
  its own photo. Reading `closest.collection.image` directly in this
  section's own Liquid isn't subject to that limitation (it's compiled
  Liquid, not an editor-bound dynamic-source setting).

  Image is deliberately left to render nothing if `closest.collection.image`
  is blank, rather than falling back to a placeholder — per instruction,
  occasion collection images are real Shopify data the client hasn't
  uploaded yet, not something to guess a filename for.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  assign occasion_collection = closest.collection
%}

<section class="lambruk-occasion-hero">
  {%- if occasion_collection.image != blank -%}
    {{
      occasion_collection.image
      | image_url: width: 2000
      | image_tag: widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 2000', sizes: '100vw', class: 'lambruk-occasion-hero__image', loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high'
    }}
  {%- endif -%}
  <div class="lambruk-occasion-hero__scrim"></div>
  <div class="lambruk-occasion-hero__content">
    <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="lambruk-occasion-hero__breadcrumb">
      {{ 'content.shop_all_products_breadcrumb' | t: occasion: occasion_collection.title }}
    </a>
    <p class="lambruk-occasion-hero__eyebrow">{{ 'content.curated_occasion' | t }}</p>
    <h1 class="lambruk-occasion-hero__title">{{ occasion_collection.title }}</h1>
    {%- if occasion_collection.description != blank -%}
      <div class="lambruk-occasion-hero__body">{{ occasion_collection.description }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  .lambruk-occasion-hero {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    min-height: 420px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #131A3E;
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-hero__image {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Deliberate departure from the design source, 2026-08-28 — the
     source specifies rgba(13, 16, 36, ...) here (the brand's own
     --blue-950 navy, confirmed identical on both breakpoints), not
     neutral black. Client call: the photography should read warm and
     natural under the scrim, not colour-shifted toward navy.

     Stops raised, 2026-09-10 — was 0.88/0.48/0.12, deliberately
     overshooting the 4.5:1 WCAG floor to a 6:1 target as headroom for
     whatever photo replaced that day's placeholders.

     Top stop raised again, 2026-09-14, 0.27 -> 0.32 -> 0.33 — the
     real photography landed (2026-09-14) and spent that headroom:
     the breadcrumb (a separate element, see its own colour note
     below) failed 4.5:1 on five of eight collection/breakpoint
     combinations against the real photos, and Entertaining/375px's
     eyebrow itself had quietly slipped under the 6:1 target even
     after the breadcrumb fix.

     0.32 was pushed first but was itself measured wrong: the reading
     was taken against the hero's own lazy-loading <img> before its
     full-resolution srcset candidate had loaded, sampling a 360x239
     placeholder in place of the real 1920x1275 photo. A corrected
     sweep -- confirming naturalWidth/naturalHeight matched the real
     asset before trusting any pixel read from it -- found 0.32 still
     left Entertaining/375px short on both counts (4.447:1 breadcrumb,
     5.998:1 eyebrow) and put the true minimum at 0.327. Set to 0.33
     for margin: 4.534:1 / 6.068:1, worst case across all eight
     collection/breakpoint combinations. Confirmed by screenshot, both
     breakpoints, all four collections -- no photo reads darker at
     0.33 than at 0.27.

     Don't lower this back toward 0.27 (or trust any number produced
     while landing on a new value for it) without re-measuring the
     eyebrow AND the breadcrumb against a freshly-loaded full-
     resolution copy of whatever image is actually in place -- reading
     a page's own <img> element the moment it scrolls into view is not
     sufficient; loading="lazy" can still be resolving to a smaller
     candidate at that instant. See DESIGN-TOKENS.md. */
  .lambruk-occasion-hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.95) 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.74) 46%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.33) 76%);
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-hero__content {
    position: relative;
    max-width: var(--page-width);
    margin-inline: auto;
    width: 100%;
    padding-inline: var(--page-margin);
    padding-block-end: 48px;
  }

  /* Deliberate departure from the design source, 2026-09-14 — both
     breakpoints specify this at 72% opacity (Desktop.dc.html:311,
     Mobile.dc.html:265, both rgba(247,245,242,.72), byte-for-byte),
     not a build invention. Raised to full opacity, matching the
     eyebrow/heading/body treatment below it, because at .72 over the
     real photography it failed 4.5:1 on five of eight collection/
     breakpoint combinations (see DESIGN-TOKENS.md and REVIEW-NOTES.md
     for the full measurement). The breadcrumb's subordination to the
     eyebrow is already carried by case, weight and tracking without
     needing the opacity too. */
  .lambruk-occasion-hero__breadcrumb {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #F7F5F2;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-hero__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #F7F5F2;
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-hero__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 26px + 2vw, 52px);
    line-height: 1.04;
    color: #F7F5F2;
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-hero__body {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: rgba(247, 245, 242, 0.84);
  }

  .lambruk-occasion-hero__body p {
    margin: 0;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.lambruk_occasion_hero",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
